Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

---

### 1. Before/after every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_MustHaveItems() { /* ... */ }
}
```

*(You can also use the constructor / `IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync` for this.)*

---

### 2. Once before first / after last test in the class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsValid() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> Class-level hooks must be **static**.

---

### 3. Once before/after all tests in the assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StartAsync();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StopAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### 4. Once for the entire test session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseHook
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### Quick-reference table

| Scope | Before | After | Method must be |
|-------|--------|-------|----------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` | Instance |
| Class (once) | `[Before(Class)]` | `[After(Class)]` | **Static** |
| Assembly (once) | `[Before(Assembly)]` | `[After(Assembly)]` | **Static** |
| Session (once) | `[Before(TestSession)]` | `[After(TestSession)]` | **Static** |

**Bonus:** `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (and `Class`/`Assembly` variants) are global cross-cutting hooks that fire for *every* test regardless of class—handy for logging or diagnostics without touching each test class.
